OL,3,GNEWSAJail and health board admit
OL,4,Acriminal charges over Covid death
OL,5,Aprisoner
OL,6,
OL,7,FA company that runs a private prison
OL,8,Fand a health board has admitted
OL,9,Fcriminal charges following the death of
OL,10,Fa prisoner who contracted Covid-19.
OL,12,FThe case is believed to be the first
OL,13,Fprosecution of its kind in the UK and
OL,14,Fcomes after the Crown Office
OL,15,Finvestigated about 6,000 deaths related
OL,16,Fto the pandemic.
OL,18,FCalum Inglis, 34, from Edinburgh, was
OL,19,Fserving a short sentence in HMP
OL,20,FAddiewell, West Lothian, for serious
OL,21,Fassault when he tested positive for
OL,22,Fcoronovirus on 12 October 2021.
OL,23,APub: 06-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  Scot NewsC Reg TVF  Weather
FL,430,420,260,160,0,100
